WEBVTT

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.360
Takeru, you did it.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.260
Soulburner won the duel.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.220
So Playmaker will get the letter.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.480
Time for me to get to work.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.480
Dad...  Mom...  Flame...

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.060
Father...

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.890
When that light vanished, so did the curse 
of your past that's been holding you down.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.900
Revolver...

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.440
You never cared about the letter, did you.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:04.880
So you could help me.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.400
Wrong.  I did it for me.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.880
That's why I fought for real.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.350
To break my own curse.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.320
Revolver...

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:23.680
Since the Dark Ignis has contacted 
Playmaker, that will probably be the final battle.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.300
It won't allow a rematch.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.870
Everything rests on Playmaker's shoulders.

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:32.770
My mission is over.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.400
Revolver...

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.240
You don't mean...

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.240
I will atone for my crimes.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:41.710
Wait!

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.760
I won't allow that.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.660
Revolver, I won't let the law judge 
you and atone for your crimes.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:59.130
You must keep watching over the network!

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.100
What do you mean?

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:06.840
When this is all over, I'm 
returning to my hometown.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.350
And I'll live there like I used to.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:24.420
Over time, people who know about 
the Lost Incident will forget it.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.360
Including me.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:32.330
There may come a day when I can live 
without remembering that incident.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.570
Soulburner...

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:40.040
That's why I won't allow you to atone for 
your crimes and forget about the incident!

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:46.010
Even if everyone forgets...  
Even if I forget...

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:49.010
You have to remember forever!

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:53.320
Both the pain and the sadness!

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.790
So that's your desire.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:56.790
Yeah.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:01.530
Then I'll start doing that.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.260
Revolver, I'm glad to have met you.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.510
Same here.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:13.140
Farewell, Soulburner and Playmaker.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.720
Playmaker, I leave the rest to you.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.190
Okay.  From here on, it's my fight.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:50.690
calling & feeling  I take your 
thoughts to heart  VRAINS

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:18.650
The data storm grazes my cheek, 
so I can't open my eyes

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:28.600
What are we trying to find?  
Where are we trying to go?

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:33.830
I won't make anyone sad anymore

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:42.380
I'll retrieve you  Let's go and look ahead

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:47.520
By meeting you, the world is in color

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:53.190
I'll protect you with an unseen bond

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:57.490
calling  With invisible wings

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:08.100
Destroy the dark and weakness within me

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.950
Takeru, you helped us a lot.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.550
Good work.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.740
Now take it easy.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.520
Thank you, Kusanagi.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.860
Did Yusaku come here afterwards?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.960
He didn't come to school today.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.660
Yeah.  He came by in the afternoon.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.630
Really?  Did he say anything?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.600
No, nothing.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.070
Are you going?

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:06.540
Yeah.  Thank you, Kusanagi.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.200
No sweat.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.500
That's it?

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:13.990
That's like him.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:17.720
I see.  He left.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:50.120
Ryoken.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.430
Farewell, Yusaku Fujiki.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:07.270
Hey, Yusaku!  Thanks for coming!

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:08.730
Ai!

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:13.970
This is the first time we meet in real life.

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:16.710
Ain't I like a human?

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:22.660
Since you came here, let 
me show you what's inside.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.180
What is this place?

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:30.320
SOL Technologies' factory.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.320
SOLtiS will be built here.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.280
What's this?

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:44.700
I'm building allies.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.670
Limited edition Ai-version SOLtiS!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.940
This is why you took over SOL Technologies?

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.650
Well, yeah.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:58.280
They'll be installed with 
free will, copied off of me.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:01.950
It won't be a perfect copy like by backup.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:06.560
But I'll spread lots of SOLtiS similar to me.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.190
Fun, right?

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.120
Then what will happen?

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:13.820
Who knows.  Even I can't predict it.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:17.670
In the beginning, they'll 
act similar to each other.

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:22.410
Revolver said that humans 
are made of flesh, right?

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.910
And those experiences 
separate humans from AI.

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:27.900
That's right.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:34.920
It won't be like humans, but they'll 
gradually think and experience different things.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:38.120
They'll rebuild themselves however they like.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:42.040
Some may do good things to humans.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:45.100
Others may do bad things.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:52.070
They may begin to have disagreements, or 
they may unite and create an AI country.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:56.660
Unexpectedly, it's hard to know my own self.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:00.040
So I don't know what will happen.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:03.010
Why are you doing this?

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:06.540
I won't be lonely anymore.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.490
Because I'm all alone right now.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:12.460
Ai, you have to stop this!

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.430
I won't, Yusaku.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:19.860
Then why did you hide a message 
for me inside Roboppi?

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:24.900
You knew Roboppi would break, 
and I would get that letter!

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:29.000
Yeah.  Roboppi's system was at its limits.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:33.910
So in the end, I gave him 
a dream world he'd enjoy.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.460
I did him wrong.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:38.880
He was a good AI.

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:44.520
Didn't you call me here to stop you?

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:45.860
Maybe.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:51.060
For better or for worse, I 
felt I should talk to you.

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:54.070
Ai, give everyone back.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:55.800
And go into hiding.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:58.100
That's not possible.

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:03.280
I set it up so that no one can 
come back unless I lose a duel.

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:04.780
Ai...

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:09.440
The copy-creation system also 
won't stop unless I lose.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:13.250
I did it so I wouldn't 
have a change of heart.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:16.490
You were planning to fight from the start.

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:20.280
Yeah.  That's the only option you have left.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.180
The rules are the same:

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:26.460
You win and survive, or I win and survive.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:32.440
We fought together so that 
we'd have to fight each other?

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:35.440
It pains me to hear you say that.

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:38.840
But I made it so that there's no going back.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.240
Ai, what happened to you?

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:42.440
Nothing special.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:46.200
In the end, I'm an AI and you're a human.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.850
We're different existences.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.820
You're walking the same path as Lightning?

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:55.260
I'm not as extreme as him.

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:57.600
I'm a bit more funny.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:00.780
I don't plan to annihilate humans.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:04.840
I only want AIs to have a chance to survive.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.810
And they choose how.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:13.810
There's no guarantee I'm opening 
Pandora's Box and courting disaster.

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:17.380
But humans may not agree.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:19.780
Because they scare easily.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:27.020
To be honest, I thought I'd 
have to fight you someday.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:29.760
You too, right?

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:33.600
If you do nothing, the 
copies will be completed.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.220
What will you do?

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:38.470
Fine.  I'll do it.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.710
That's the spirit.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:42.440
Here I go, Ai!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:43.860
Yeah!

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.380
Into the VRAINS!

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:01.500
Duel!

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:04.600
My turn!

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.730
I summon Garbage Collector!

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:13.680
I activate the Continuous 
Spell, Cynet Optimization!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:18.380
Due to its effect, I summon Flame Bufferlo!

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:23.480
Garbage Collector's effect activates!

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:27.620
I return a different Cyberse to my hand...

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:34.000
...to Special Summon a Cyberse from my deck 
with the same Level but different name!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.030
I return Flame Bufferlo to my hand.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.230
I Special Summon Sea Archiver!

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.820
I activate Flame Bufferlo's effect!

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:49.400
When it's faceup and leaves the field...

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:54.150
...I discard a Cyberse from my hand 
and draw two cards from my deck.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.080
I Link Summon!

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:00.080
Link 2 Splash Mage!

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:03.220
Splash Mage's effect activates!

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:07.230
I Special Summon a Cyberse from 
my graveyard in defense position!

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:10.230
Resurrect, Sea Archiver!

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:12.660
Then I Link Summon!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.500
Appear, Link 3!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.340
Decode Talker!

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:27.140
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:37.090
Decode Talker...  The first Link 
Monster we acquired together.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:43.060
Ai, you made me search for 
the Cyberse Deck, didn't you.

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:52.880
What are you talking about?

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:54.980
The Hanoi were chasing me.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:58.280
I was on the run, which led me to you.

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:02.380
I knew you were my partner, 
so I sought your help.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:06.480
No, you've been observing me the whole time.

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:12.890
During the five years you were on the run 
from the Hanoi, after they attacked the Cyberse.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:18.760
You were influencing my 
life from the shadows.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:29.040
Not a big, overt influence.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:35.180
A little something that I saw or heard.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.950
That's what you kept doing.

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:41.920
To lead me on the path of 
revenge against the Hanoi.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.240
And not just me.

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:49.590
Also Kusanagi.

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:55.570
Making sure we wouldn't notice, you led 
us both to Den City and LINK VRAINS.

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:04.080
You knew that Kusanagi and 
I would eventually meet.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:12.800
You gave me the Cyberse Deck so that I 
would protect you and defeat the Hanoi.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.720
Am I wrong?

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:20.020
Impressive.  You noticed everything.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:24.030
That's right.  I gave you your weapon.

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:29.230
The Cyberse Deck that symbolizes Playmaker.

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:35.970
As I expected, you grew and 
defeated the annoying Hanoi.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.910
Everything was premediated?

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.950
What a sad thing to say.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:44.920
Well, it was like that in the beginning.

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.820
But it's different now.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:50.320
You're my only friend.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:54.040
And you're fine losing your only friend?

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.630
Maybe.

00:16:55.980 --> 00:17:00.200
Show me how much you've grown!

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.100
Here I go!

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:02.730
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:05.700
I summon Pikari!

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.580
Pikari's effect activates!

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:11.910
I add Ignister A.I.Land 
from my deck to my hand!

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:13.380
Link Summon!

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.620
Link 1 Linguriboh!

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:21.720
I activate the Field 
Spell, Ignister A.I.Land!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:26.640
I Special Summon a Level 4 or 
below @Ignister from my hand!

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:31.860
The Special Summoned 
Doyon's effect activates!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:35.130
I add Pikari from my graveyard to my hand!

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:39.380
I activate the Continuous 
Spell, CompromA.I.se!

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:44.720
Once per turn, I treat an @Ignister 
as a Continuous Spell...

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:49.010
...and place it faceup 
in my Spell & Trap Zone!

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:52.480
You changed a monster into a spell card.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:56.450
Ignister A.I.Land's effect activates again!

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.460
Appear, Pikari!

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:03.220
Pikari's effect activates!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:07.670
I add a second Ignister A.I.Land 
from my deck to my hand.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:11.900
I activate the Continuous 
Spell, CompromA.I.se's effect!

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:15.960
Once per turn, when a monster 
is Special Summoned...

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:20.140
...I Special Summon an @Ignister 
from my Spell & Trap Zone!

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:24.160
Return to the Main Monster Zone, Doyon!

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:28.750
Appear!  The circuit that guides the dark!

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:32.760
The creation of dark shadows!

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:35.520
The wisdom of the dark night 
scatters throughout the world!

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:39.730
Gather in my hand to become 
the power of rising vigor!

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:41.260
Link Summon!

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:46.880
Appear, Link 3 Dark Templar @Ignister!

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:52.940
Ignister A.I.Land's effect activates!

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.520
I Special Summon Achichi from my hand!

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:03.120
When a monster is Special Summoned
 next to a  Link Monster's link,

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.400
Dark Templar's effect activates!

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:10.060
I Special Summon Pikari and 
Doyon next to its links!

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.500
Appear!  The circuit that guides the dark!

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:22.070
With high spirits, the soul 
resurrects from the river of fire!

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:25.440
Become red hot and burn!

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:31.420
Appear, Link 3 Fire Phoenix @Ignister!

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:33.940
Here I go, Playmaker.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.490
I'll show you how determined I am!

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:39.390
I activate this card!

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.260
That's right.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:46.300
A card that shows how 
determined I am to fight you!

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:59.140
The three arrows that judge everything!

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:01.110
Judgment Arrows!

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.580
Ai...

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:05.520
Here I go, Playmaker!  Battle!

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:11.720
But the Continuous Spell, Cynet Optimization 
is already active on my field!

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:19.460
So when my Code Talker battles, you 
can't activate your cards' effects!

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:25.060
Oh, so you already have a counterstrategy 
against my @Ignister.

00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:26.870
But I won't stop!

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:31.440
Fire Phoenix attacks Decode Talker!

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:35.350
I won't let you!

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:38.400
I activate the Continuous Trap, Code Hack!

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.680
Effects can't destroy Code 
Talkers on the field!

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:47.360
And once per turn, when 
a Code Talker battles...

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:52.360
...your monster's ATK become 0 during battle!

00:20:54.570 --> 00:21:01.540
The monsters also aren't destroyed in 
battle, and both our battle damage become 0!

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.110
So that's your move.  I see.

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:06.540
You won't allow mutual destruction.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:11.480
Then I'll attack Decode 
Talker with Dark Templar!

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:14.490
Code Hack can only be used once per turn.

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:17.470
So Dark Templar's ATK don't decrease!

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:20.580
The two monsters' ATK are equal.

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:25.200
But Dark Templar can't be destroyed in 
battle against a monster with equal ATK!

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:29.500
How unfortunate.

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:35.120
If I could use Dark Templar's effect, 
I could've resurrected @Ignister.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:41.380
Code Hack's effect now ends, so Fire 
Phoenix's ATK return to normal.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:47.080
I set one card and end my turn.

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:51.340
Hey.  You no longer have any monsters.

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:55.060
With this turn, you now 
realize how serious I am.

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:57.900
I'll show no mercy in this duel.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:22:00.660
Take this seriously, or you'll die instantly.

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:01.820
Ai!

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:09.260
I was told repeatedly

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:16.710
Only tales of dreams

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:23.700
Is my life precious?

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:26.670
Make up for  Make up for

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:34.180
The next sentimental

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.440
I'm not a machine

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:51.880
I cry a single tear

